+# Native Creator Kit helper
+
+This workspace target delegates capture and instantiation to `engine::creator_kit`. The native engine owns typed request parsing, scratch Sessions, template import, source clocks, editable effects/audio, and project serialization. The existing workspace `apps/*` membership discovers the helper.
+
+The selected Windows workspace helper built with `cargo build --release --locked --offline -p clipline-creator-kit`. All 31 native API boundary tests passed. An actual product canonical-caller replay then created and published two moments from the same pinned Kit/source/template assets and verified nondefault static audio settings after exact native reopen. These results establish the tested creation boundary; binary distribution, GUI integration, long-duration performance, arbitrary Kit properties/assets, and Kit updates remain separate gates. Preserved native audio fields do not establish rendered DSP/sample behavior.
+
+The helper accepts only:
+
+```text
+clipline-creator-kit capture SEED PROFILE_JSON NEW_TEMPLATE
+clipline-creator-kit instantiate REQUEST_JSON NEW_PROJECT
+```
+
+It reads bounded JSON bytes and delegates document creation to the native owner. The canonical caller admits explicit Moment/Kit/source/template records, owns the gated process and verifies compact creation receipts. Successful files require ProjectStore publication. Creation receipts do not overwrite canonical records or become later timeline authority. Stderr, nonzero exits, partial outputs and unknown process/publication states require explicit reconciliation; the helper adds no automatic retry, command registry, general batch API or Python timeline.
